USER To answer your questions: (1) The 'get_or_derive' function should be called outside the 'derive' function. This means that the 'AsymmetricEncryptionKey' struct should hold a reference to the actual private key and credential. You may also include a reference to the identites to derive the store key, but I think it is easier if you just include the store key directly in the struct. Note that this struct will be private and only meant to be used to abstract the behavior of recovering previously computed values from the store. (2) Lets ignore that for now. Can you update your plan?
